# /etc/agent-sandbox-exec/denylist — root-controlled base list (cluster-wide).
# Per-user additions go in ~/.config/agent-sandbox-exec/denylist.
#
# Files the sandboxed agents (claude / codex / kimi / glm) must NOT read, nor
# any subprocess they spawn (cat | pipe, hardlinks, cp source -- all blocked at
# open by the BPF-LSM, returning EPERM).
#
# Format:
#   - one absolute path per line
#   - regular FILES only (no directories, no globs)
#   - blank lines and lines starting with '#' are ignored
#   - each file must exist (agent-sandbox-execd stats it -> inode)
#   - symlink entries in the HOME list are rejected (base list follows them)
#
# Reloading: a uid's list is re-read on every launch and diff-applied to its
# cgroup, so edits take effect on the next launch — no daemon restart needed.
# Restart agent-sandbox-execd only to refresh a sandbox that is already running
# and issues no new launch.
#
# Examples (uncomment a line to enable):
# /home/owner/.ssh/id_rsa
# /home/owner/.aws/credentials
